## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of edge-resilience architecture, cross-region signal fusion, and automated rollback under production pressure.

## Key Concepts
- Edge routing and regional health checks
- Synthetic monitoring and traffic shaping
- Degraded-mode caching (stale-while-revalidate)
- Canary deployments and safe rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
function selectDegradedRoute(region, originHealth) {
  if (originHealth[region] === 'degraded') {
    return 'degradedRoute';
  }
  return 'normalRoute';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect a degraded origin earlier in the request lifecycle?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to handle clock skew and scheduling drift in a regulated batch pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- Clock synchronization, idempotent batch processing, per-tenant isolation
- Safe backfill, read-after-write consistency, and rollback criteria
- Clear observability and thresholds for cross-region workloads

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo dedupe example
async function processBatch(batchId, tenantId, payload){
  const key = `${batchId}:${tenantId}`;
  const exists = await redis.setnx(`dedup:${key}`, '1');
  if(!exists) return; // already processed
  // process
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the backfill strategy without impacting live tenants?
- What if clock drift persists after NTP sync—what changes to the plan would you add?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical mastery of deduplication in real systems, combining transactional patterns, Kafka exactly-once semantics, and robust auditing.

## Key Concepts

- Exactly-once processing
- Transactional outbox pattern
- Kafka transactions (transactional.id)
- Idempotency keys and dedupe stores
- Compensating actions and audit trails

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: within a DB transaction
BEGIN;
UPDATE orders SET status='PAID' WHERE id = :orderId;
INSERT INTO outbox (order_id, event_type, payload, created_at) VALUES (:orderId, 'OrderPaid', :payload, NOW());
COMMIT;
```

```javascript
// Kafka publish path (conceptual)
producer.beginTransaction();
producer.send(outboxEvent);
producer.commitTransaction();
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you simulate duplicates under failure modes (partition revocation, broker failure)?
- What metrics and logs would you instrument to verify end-to-end exactly-once behavior?
